Solar System Observatory / 太阳系动态观测台

This project bundles or loads third-party materials that remain under their
own terms. They are NOT relicensed by any license chosen for the project's own
source code. The per-file ledger is THIRD_PARTY_ASSETS.md.

Third-party attributions
------------------------
- Spacecraft and small-body 3D models: NASA 3D Resources
  (https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/) and NASA VTAD. Some files are
  web-optimized derivatives (e.g. Meshopt/WebP compression).
- Comet 67P shape model: ESA / Rosetta, 67P Shape Models v2.0
  (https://doi.org/10.26007/34vg-8s07).
- Apophis shape model: NASA PDS / JPL Radar Shape Model v1.0.
- Arrokoth shape model: NASA PDS / Porter (2024)
  (https://doi.org/10.26007/97r3-1e19).
  Science meshes were converted to compact GLB files.
- Ephemerides and orbital data: NASA/JPL Horizons, JPL Approximate Positions
  of the Major Planets, and the JPL Small-Body Database.
- Sun, Mercury, Venus, Earth (incl. clouds), Mars and Jupiter textures:
  Solar System Scope (https://www.solarsystemscope.com/textures/), CC BY 4.0,
  based on NASA data.
- Milky Way panorama: ESO / S. Brunier
  (https://www.eso.org/public/images/eso0932a/), CC BY 4.0.
- Saturn, Uranus, Neptune, Pluto and Saturn-ring textures: threex.planets,
  derived from Planet Pixel Emporium; used under that source's terms.
- Moon texture: three.js example asset.
- Fonts (loaded from Google Fonts): Noto Sans SC, Orbitron, Space Mono,
  SIL Open Font License 1.1.
- The Tiangong models are project-authored reconstructions from public
  CMSA/CNSA references; they are not official engineering CAD.

